course: dictionary
lesson: 10095
title: One word, many meanings: thick
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. Thick is a good example. Read the words around it first. «Penguins also keep warm with a thick layer of fat» means the layer is deep from one side to the other, so thick is about distance.
explain: «Thick fog» is different. Fog is hard to see through, so thick here means fog that hides things. Same word, new meaning. Ask yourself: what is being described, and what would it do? The thing tells you the sense.
explain: Thick can also mean slow to understand, but this is informal and can be rude. «Thick as two short planks» is a British joke, and it is not a kind thing to say about a person. In sentences about measuring, cooking or science, thick has a plain, careful meaning.
explain: Use the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence. If «thick soup» means soup that does not flow easily, the sentence still makes sense. If it does not fit, try another meaning.
fact: Thick means having a large distance between two sides, as in «a thick book» or «a thick wall».
fact: Thick can mean growing close together, as in «a thick forest».
fact: A thick liquid does not flow easily. Scientists call this viscous, like honey.
fact: Thick fog or smoke is hard to see through, and in a fire you should stay low.
fact: Informally, thick means slow to understand. It is rude, so avoid using it about people.
exercise: «Penguins also keep warm with a thick layer of fat and tightly packed waterproof feathers.» What does thick mean here? | Slow to understand | *A large distance from one side to the other | Growing close together | Hard to see through
exercise: Dad says the honey is too thick to pour. What does thick mean? | *A liquid that does not flow easily | Slow to understand | Hard to see through | Growing close together
exercise: «Darwin's finches have beaks shaped for different foods, thick for seeds and thin for insects.» In this sentence, what does thin mean? | Thick in a big way | Growing close together | *Narrow, with a small distance between its two sides | Hard to see through
test: «Thick fog hid the path.» What does thick mean in this sentence? | *Hard to see through | Very cold | Growing close together | Very heavy
test: Which phrase means in good and bad times? | *Through thick and thin | Thick as two short planks | Thick as thieves | In the thick of
exam: «Thick as two short planks» is a British joke. What does thick mean in this phrase? | *Slow to understand, said informally and rudely | Hard to see through | Growing close together | Very tall and strong
